(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #158: a format string as the match of `treating` is the
 text it builds, so it fires over a text list exactly as a text does.)

a text called word is "kiwi".
a text called fruit is "fig".
print each name from ["kiwi", "lime"] treating "{word}" as "matched".
print each name from ["kiwi", "lime"] treating word as "matched".
print each name from ["kiwi", "big fig"] treating "big {fruit}" as "large".
a list called basket is ["lime", "kiwi"].
a list called sorted is [].
append each name from basket treating "{word}" as "found" to sorted.
Print "{sorted}".

To announce with a text called item.
    Print "announced {item}".

announce of each name from basket treating "{word}" as "the kiwi".

To 'sort the basket' with a list called crate.
    print each name from crate treating "{word}" as "matched in a function".

'sort the basket' with basket.
